Article published in "The Letters of Nations"

				UNCONDITIONAL SURRENDER OF KATZARIN


After the sensational defeat of General Karpov on Katzar
ground, nothing more could stop the armoured tanks of
% & in their race to the capital
of Katzarin : Markoul the red.
It was under the inflexible gaze of &
that the dictator Goumir Kratov signed the act of total and
unconditional surrender of Katzarin. Finding it hard to
withhold his hatred, Kratov threw his pen down on the table
and uttered an icy "there", before regaining his cell where
he is awaiting the date of his court hearing. There they
will judge him for crimes committed by the Katzar army on
the Littlestonian population.


The Honourable President, Claris Jackson, didn't wait for
the return of & before offering to him the rank
of General in Chief of the Armies and the post of Military
Consultant for the Government.

It is a euphoric capital which is preparing for the return
of the triumphant hero who will receive from the hands of
the same honourable President the highest distinctions :
The Baton ofthe Grand Commander of Nations.

This day, which will stay in the history of our country,
has been declared National Day of Liberty.

                                         Dan Rubitch.